    "definitions": {
      "short": "aid",
      "usage": "help(-ed, -er).",
      "full": "H5833. ezrah or ezrath I. עֶזְרָ֫תָה עֶזְרָת, עֶזְרָה, noun feminine help, succour, assistance ; — absolute ׳ע Isa 10:3 +, עֶזְרָת Psalm 60:13; Psa 108:13 (Ges § 80g ), עֶזְרָ֫תָה 63:8 2 t.; construct עֶזְרַת Isa 31:2 +; suffix עֶזְרָתִי Psa 22:20 +, etc.; — 1 help, succour Isa 10:3 ; 20:6 (+ לְהִנָּצֵל ), 31:1 ; Jer 37:7 ; Lam 4:17 ; Job 6:13 ; 2Chr 28:21 ; ׳ע אָ֑וֶן מֹּעֲלֵי Isa 31:2 help from , etc.; ׳ע ׳י Judg 5:23 (twice in verse) help of (for) ׳י ; from ׳י Psa 22:20 ; Psalm 38:23; 40:14 (|| לְהַצִּילֵנִי ), 70:2 (|| id. ), 71:12 + מִצָּ֑ר Psalm 60:13 (|| תְּשׁוּעָה ) = 108:13 . 2 concrete, embodied help, one who helps (compare 1 עֵזֶר 2 ): a. collective Job 31:21 when I saw my help (assistance, support) in the gate; ׳בֵּע (see I. עֵזֶר 2 ) Nahum 3:9 . b. of ׳י Psa 27:9 ; Psalm 40:18 (+ מְפַלֵּט ), 46:2 (|| עֹז מַחֲסֶה, ) Psalm 44:27; 63:8 ; 94:17 ; ׳בְּע 35:2 .",
      "rootNote": "or עֶזְרָת ; (Psalm 60:11 (13); Psalm 108:12 (13)), feminine of 5828 ;",
